v 3
d 'ESREG': module to estimate the endogenous switching regression with heterogeneous selection on gains
d
d  esreg estimates the endogenous switching regression (the Roy model with
d  two regimes): a probit selection equation and an outcome equation for each
d  regime, by full-information maximum likelihood or by a two-step estimator
d  whose variance is that of the whole procedure (stacked moments). It
d  reports the treatment effects ATT, ATU and ATE and the selection on gains,
d  kappa = rho1 sigma1 - rho0 sigma0, constant or heterogeneous in the
d  covariates (kappa(x)), with standard errors from the influence functions
d  of the whole procedure (the estimation of the parameters, the averaging
d  over the units and their covariance), by observation, by cluster or
d  through the survey design (svyset: the svy prefix for the likelihood,
d  vce(svy) for the two-step). An augmented two-step adds Hermite terms, in
d  both regimes or in one, when the conditional mean of the regime errors is
d  not linear. A family of post-estimation commands checks the assumptions
d  one by one: esrdiag (strength, variation and support of the selection
d  equation), esrtest (specification of the index, sufficiency of the
d  instruments, constant kappa, normality by regime, and a pseudo-difference-
d  in-differences on the index), esrcurve (the effect by quantile group of
d  the score), esrmte (the marginal treatment effect, parametric and
d  semiparametric) and esrreport (a reading of the results and the route to
d  report). A dialog box and help examples run from clickable links are
d  included. The commands are validated against etregress, movestay, msat and
d  a Python reference implementation, and their standard errors against
d  brute-force influence functions. A technical note documents the model, the
d  tests and the estimators; it is included as an ancillary file
d  (esreg_technical_note.pdf) and on Zenodo:
d  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22717028
d
d KW: endogenous switching regression
d KW: Roy model
d KW: treatment effects
d KW: selection on gains
d KW: marginal treatment effect
d KW: control function
d KW: survey design
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261003
d
d Author: Abdelkrim Araar, Universite Laval and Partnership for Economic Policy (PEP)
d Support: email aabd@ecn.ulaval.ca
d
d (A copy of the package as submitted to the SSC archive, version 1.0.0, to
d test it before SSC publishes it: the example data and the other ancillary
d files are copied to the current folder by net get.)
d
